✅ Types of Cloud

Public Cloud – Services offered over the public internet, shared across multiple customers.
Private Cloud – Dedicated infrastructure for a single organization.
Hybrid Cloud – Combination of public and private cloud environments.


✅ Major Cloud Service Providers

AWS (Amazon Web Services)
Microsoft Azure
Google Cloud Platform (GCP)


✅ Key Differences Between Cloud Providers

Implementation – How services are deployed and managed.
Scalability – Ability to scale resources up/down efficiently.
Performance – Speed, latency, and reliability of services.
Security – Compliance, encryption, and identity management.


✅ Google Cloud Platform (GCP) Overview

Free Tier Account:

Requires a credit card for signup.
Includes limited free usage of GCP services.


Enterprise Account:

Designed for organizations using Google Workspace.
Structure:
Organization → Folder → Projects → Resources



Free Account Structure:
GCP → Free Account → Projects → GCP Services
Enterprise Account Structure:
GCP → Organization (Workspace) → Folder → Projects → Resources

